# `COPY . /r-benchmarks` must not carry the host's working state into the image.
#
# benchmarks/**/data/ matters most: those are the five `.rds` caches a setup()
# writes on first run, ~380 MB on a developer machine. Copying them in would both
# bloat the image and hide the very failure CI exists to catch -- a benchmark
# whose doctor() only passes because a stale cache happens to be on disk.
benchmarks/**/data/
benchmarks/marker.o
benchmarks/marker.so

.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
output*/

.git/
.github/
ci/
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
